{
  "format": "contentrain-menu-parity@1",
  "origin": "https://example.test",
  "about": "Block-theme menus (wp_navigation posts and inline navigation in template parts) → RawMenu, as both @contentrain/wp-import (rest-menus.ts) and the Contentrain Bridge (Menus::from_blocks) export them. Owned by wp-import; the Bridge copies this file unchanged and pins the commit it copied.",
  "rules": [
    "`origin` is the site's home. Each side runs against its own home and reads it as `origin`: an address on its own home compares as one on `origin`.",
    "`public` is what the importer read and proved public: published, unprotected posts of any type (with their public `link`) and terms. Anything else (a draft, a private or password-protected post, one never read) is not public. `parts` are all template parts with their area; `templates` are the site's templates; `navigations` are wp_navigation posts, and only `status: publish` ones are menus. `taken` are slugs classic menus already use.",
    "Only template parts a template uses count; without templates, the part whose slug is its area. A part used inside a part is opened in place, once. A navigation block's `ref` gives that navigation the part's area; an empty one without `ref` shows the most recent published navigation (by `date_gmt`, then id).",
    "Menus come in this order: navigation posts by id, then inline navigations by area (header, footer, others) and document order. A navigation post's slug is its own, or `navigation-<id>` without one, suffixed `-nav` while taken; an inline menu is named by its `ariaLabel` or `<Area> navigation[ N]`, its slug suffixed `-2`, `-3` while taken.",
    "A link to a post or term the site states (block `id`, or a same-site `?page_id=` / `?p=` typed by hand, `www.` or not) is checked: not public → left out and counted in `dropped`, its children moving up to its parent. A public one points at its public `link`, whatever address the block kept.",
    "A page list lists the public pages under `parentPageID` (0 by default) as a tree, by `menu_order` then title. A home link is `<origin>/`, labelled `Home` when it has no label. A site-relative address is made absolute; `#` stays `#`.",
    "`expect.menus[].items` compares title (tags stripped, entities decoded, whitespace collapsed), url, and `parent` as the titles of its ancestors, outermost first. Ids, order numbers, targets and classes are each side's own. `locations` is absent when a navigation is shown nowhere."
  ],
